# Day 6 – APT

# What I Learned
  - How to install, update, remove and search programs.
    
# Commands Practiced
  - `sudo apt update`
  - `sudo apt upgrade`
  - `sudo apt install name`
  - `sudo apt remove name`
  - `apt list --install` and its different version
  - `apt show name`
  - `apt search htop`
  - `which "program name"
    
# What I Understood in Simple Words
  - how to update apt repo and upgrade installed packages
  - how to install and remove programms
  - how to list installed programms along with adding filters using |grep or only head lines with |head
  - with apt show we can see lot of info about the package from apt repo
  - which command show the path of installed program
  - search command show all the programs containing the asked string
    
# Problems I Faced
  - update showed >2100 packages are upgradable
  - apt list --installed shows a warning about not using this command in scripts and then nothing
  - apt show tells a lot about the package from apt repo
  - which shows program not found
  - search shows a lot and not good for something specific
    
# How I Fixed Them 
  - run upgrade command only when needed
  - showing nothing means not installed
  - to see if its installed look for a headed saying APT-Installed: yes, if its missing then package is not installed
  - that means package not installed
  - use show, list, and which to see the info about particular package
    
